^SAMPLE = GSM4237499
!Sample_title = data1_H820_D0
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM4237499
!Sample_status = Public on Nov 30 2020
!Sample_submission_date = Dec 27 2019
!Sample_last_update_date = Dec 01 2020
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = CRISPR Screening
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype/treatment: Wild type (day 0)
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: NCI-H820
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = The third portion cultured with erlotinib for 7 (E7) or 14 days (E14). Erlotinib treated cells and control cells were passaged in fresh media with and without erlotinib, respectively (media changed in every 2-3 days). The screening experiment was performed in duplicate. All samples were subjected to sgRNA sequencing as follows.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Freshly prepared NCI-H820 cells (~2 × 107 cells) containing GeCKO libraries were split into three plates with each portion containing a minimum of 3 x 106 cells. The first portion were frozen down for genomic DNA analysis to profile the sgRNA diversity after transfection (D0) and  the second portion cultured in DMSO without erlotinib for 7 (D7) or 14 days (D14) as control samples.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Frozen cell pellets were thawed and genomic DNA was extracted with a Blood & Cell Culture Midi kit (Qiagen).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The amplification of sgRNA target sequences for deep sequencing was performed as described (http://genome-engineering.org/gecko) with minor modifications. All PCR products obtained from each sample were run on an agarose gel, gel-extracted, and purified according to manufacturer’s recommendations.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = sgRNA (RNA-seq)
!Sample_description = data1
!Sample_description = sgRNA
!Sample_data_processing = Raw read data was first run through quality control metrics using FastQC.
!Sample_data_processing = Sequenced reads were filtered low quality sequence using fastx tool kit.
!Sample_data_processing = Resulting reads were trimmed to remove the constant portion of the sgRNA sequences with CRISPR.sgRNA_read_trimmer in the GenePattern Module Archive, then aligned to the GeCKO v2 sgRNA library using bowtie 1 (v1.1.1) under default settings.
!Sample_data_processing = After alignment, the number of uniquely aligned reads for each library sequence was calculated by CRISPR.single_sgRNA_count in GParc.
!Sample_data_processing = The raw read counts were normalized as follows: normalized reads per sgRNA = (reads per sgRNA / total reads for all sgRNAs in sample) x 10^6 + 1.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: hg19
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: csv file include raw read count
!Sample_platform_id = GPL16791
!Sample_contact_name = AHYOUNG,,CHOI
